  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\nI'm using the very nice docker image of synapse and would like to follow the default configuration and only override specific parts of it. It seems that synapse supports config fragments in a directory (which the debian package seems to be [using](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/debian/matrix-synapse.service#L10) ), but the docker image runs [start.py](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/docker/start.py#L250) which doesn't have the relevant flags and doesn't allow passing them in.",
